\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens\b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2012\par 22:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher on Monday, as a number of shares moved in opposite directions during a session with light trading.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index closed 0.59% higher at 20,592.42.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index ended 0.3% stronger at 28,558.12.\par \par \uc2 Peru's biggest engineering and property company, Grana y Montero SAA (GRAMONC1.VL), increased 0.9% to finish at 6.90 soles ($2.56).\par \par \uc2 Canadian gold producer \uc2 Rio Alto Mining\uc2  (RIOAF, RIO.V) gained 0.6% to close at $3.68.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way were precious-metals mining company \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.VL), which lost 0.9% to end at $39.50.\par \par \uc2 Tin mining company \uc2 Minsur SA\uc2  (MINSURI1.VL) declined 0.4% to end at PEN2.76.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday to buy $2 million at an average of PEN2.692 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol closed stronger on Monday at PEN2.693 to the dollar from PEN2.695 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the sol has appreciated 0.15% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Ryan Dube, \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\uc2 ; 51-945 043 802; peru@dowjones.com [ 16-01-12 2121GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120116e81g00151\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
