\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's sol gains 4 pct on year, outperforms peers\b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2011\par 20:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Dec 29 (Reuters) - Peru's sol strengthened 4 percent against the dollar in 2011 after closing at 2.697 on Thursday, its last trading day of the year, bucking a trend in Latin America where most of its peers lost ground.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso , Chile's peso, and Brazil's real each lost about 10 percent this year. The pesos of Colombia and Argentina also lost ground.\par \par \uc2 The sol gained this year even though \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb volatility, mostly by buying up dollars.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sidestepped fallout from a presidential election in June. Ollanta Humala, a former military officer, was elected by running as a moderate leftist and shedding a hardline image that had rattled markets during his first presidential bid in 2006. He has since been embraced by Peru's business community for keeping conservative economic policymakers in their posts.\par \par \uc2 During periodic bouts of hot-money inflows in the region since 2008, Peru's sol has usually appreciated less than its peers, partly because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has limited the ability of investors to park short-term cash in the country. That means the sol also has less ground to lose during periods of swift outflows.\par \par \uc2 Peru's economy grew nearly 7 percent this year and is expected to expand more than 5 percent next year as hot domestic demand offsets a potentially softer market for its metals exports.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting By Ursula Scollo and Terry Wade; Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-PERU/SOL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120101e7ct000c1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
