\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Strengthens\b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2011\par 22:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended lower Tuesday, as various mining companies lost ground.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index ended 0.75% lower at 19,587.19. The blue-chip Selective Index closed 0.57% weaker at 27,476.77.\par \par \uc2 Precious-metals company \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.VL) lost 0.8% to finish at $37.40.\par \par \uc2 Tin miner \uc2 Minsur SA\uc2  (MINSURI1.VL) fell 1.43% to end at 2.76 soles ($1.02).\par \par \uc2 Base metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) tumbled 6.33% to close at $29.60, following a downgrade by Barclay's Capital, which pointed to rising project execution risks in Peru. Barclay's said in a report Tuesday it lowered its price target for Southern Copper to $32 per share from $34, while downgrading its rating to 3-underweight from 2-equal weight.\par \par \uc2 "In our view, exogenous factors such as political developments and social unrest in Peru pose a threat to the company, and will likely lead market observers to adjust volume expectations," Barclay's said. "We believe the volatile situation in \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  warrants caution."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday to buy $211 million at an average of PEN2.695 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. In total, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased $1.06 billion in December. The sol has strengthened in recent days as companies buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay taxes and bonuses for workers.\par \par \uc2 The sol closed stronger Tuesday at PEN2.696 per dollar, compared to PEN2.7 in the previous session. So far this year, the sol has appreciated 3.95% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -By Ryan Dube, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-945 043 802; peru@dowjones.com [ 13-12-11 2139GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111213e7cd0018l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
