\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2011\par 22:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended lower Wednesday as various mining companies lost ground.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's General Index fell 0.52% to end at 19,986.43.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index declined 0.17% to close at 27,998.48.\par \par \uc2 Base metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO, SCCO.VL) declined 0.94% to finish at $31.50, as copper prices decreased.\par \par \uc2 Tin miner \uc2 Minsur SA\uc2  (MINSURI1.VL) fell 0.35% to end at 2.85 soles ($1.06).\par \par \uc2 Canadian gold producer \uc2 Rio Alto Mining\uc2  (RIO) fell 3.27% to close at $3.25. Rio Alto said on Dec. 1 that it is on track to produce 50,000 ounces of gold this year at its La Arena mine in northern Peru. Production at the mine began in May.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) ended 1.39% lower at $106.50. The company owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday to buy $123 million at an average of PEN2.696 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $537 million. On Monday it purchased $43 million, and on Tuesday it bought $101 million.\par \par \uc2 Peru's sol has appreciated in recent days as companies buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay taxes and bonuses for workers.\par \par \uc2 The sol closed unchanged Wednesday at PEN2.697 per dollar.\par 