\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes End Mixed; Sol Strengthens\b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2011\par 22:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended mixed Monday, as a rise in a number of blue chip shares was offset by a decline in \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's general index rose 0.11%, to end at 20,200.38.\par \par \uc2 The selective blue chip index decreased 0.02%, to finish at 28,209.12.\par \par \uc2 Precious-metals company \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.VL) gained 1.08%, to end at $37.50, while base metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) increased 1.46%, to end at $31.20, as the price of copper improved.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 ., (BAP) which owns Peru's largest bank, rose 0.18%, to end at $110.20.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way was silver and lead miner \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA, (VOLCABC1.VL), which lost 3.10%, to end at 3.10 soles ($1.15) in heavy trade.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday to buy $43 million at an average of PEN2.6975 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $537 million.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol closed slightly stronger Monday, at PEN2.698 per dollar, compared to PEN2.699 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the sol has appreciated 3.88% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-99927 7269; peru@dowjones.com [ 12-05-11 1627ET ]\