\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-Peru's key rate seen held steady at 4.25 pct\b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2011\par 20:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WHAT: Peru interest rate decision\par \par \uc2 WHEN: Thursday, Nov. 10, around 6 p.m. EST (2300 GMT)\par \par \uc2 OUTCOME: 14 of 14 analysts see rate steady at 4.25 percent\par \par \uc2 REUTERS FORECAST: Economists polled by Reuters unanimously expect Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold the benchmark interest rate steady at 4.25 percent on Thursday for the sixth straight month citing the ongoing global economic uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added a sentence to its September policy statement implying it would cut the benchmark rate if the global economic outlook deteriorated. Europe is embroiled in a debt crisis and growth is slowing in the United States and China, key markets for Peru's exports.\par \par \uc2 But inflation rose a higher-than-expected 0.31 percent in October, making a rate cut unlikely this month. All 14 economists surveyed by Reuters said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would maintain the rate at 4.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say a large global economic shock, such as an eventual debt default from Greece, could eventually prompt Peru to cut its interest rate.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, the local economy is posting strong growth, and gross domestic product expanded 7.49 percent in August. The economy is expected go grow around 6 around percent this year after accelerating nearly 9 percent in 2010.\par \par \uc2 MARKET IMPACT: Seen minimal. A higher or lower interest rate could boost or decrease the demand for Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol, but the sol has strengthened steadily in October and November and is trading around its strongest levels in more than three years even though rates have been on hold.\par \par \uc2 The sol <PEN=PE> closed bidding flat at 2.703 soles per U.S. dollar on the local spot market on Tuesday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $140 million in an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 PERU\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/RATES (PREVIEW)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111111e7b8001w4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
