\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens\b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2011\par 21:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Monday following gains on Wall Street due to reports that Italian Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi will resign.\par \par \uc2 The broad General Index ended 0.63% higher at 19,515.20.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index closed 0.68% stronger at 27,259.21.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP), the owner of Peru's largest bank Banco de Credito, increased 2.44% to end at $109.10.\par \par \uc2 Base metals mining company \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) rose 4.29% to close at $32.85.\par \par \uc2 Silver and lead miner \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLCABC1.VL) gained 1.12% to end at 2.72 soles ($1.01).\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday to buy $140 million at an average of PEN2.703 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $2 million at an average of PEN2.704 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The sol closed slightly stronger on Tuesday at PEN2.704 per dollar, compared with PEN2.705 per dollar in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the sol has appreciated 3.67% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Ryan Dube, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-945 043 802; peru@dowjones.com [ 11-08-11 1536ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020111108e7b8000nu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
