\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2011\par 21:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended slightly higher Monday, while various blue-chip shares moved in opposite directions.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index closed 0.04% higher at 19,378.95.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index ended 0.04% stronger at 27,079.34.\par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.VL) gained 4.3% to end at $44.85, as gold closed at a six-week high on the Comex division of the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Peruvian copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 1.41% to close at $36.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way was financial holding \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP), which declined 1.83% to end at $107. The company owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.\par \par \uc2 Base metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) fell 1.25% to close at $31.50.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday to buy $2 million at an average of PEN2.704 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 The sol closed unchanged Monday at PEN2.705 per dollar. So far this year, the sol has appreciated 3.63% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Ryan Dube, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-945 043 802; peru@dowjones.com [ 11-07-11 1549ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020111107e7b7000pr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
