\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2011\par 22:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended lower Monday, as key blue chips continued to sell off, following a downturn in U.S. markets.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index closed down 2.67% at 17,838.98. The blue-chip Selective Index ended 2.67% lower at 24,869.87.\par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.Vl) fell 0.92% to end at $37.60.\par \par \uc2 Base metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 .(SCCO) fell 1.84% to end at $24.50, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA(CVERDEC1.VL) lost 2.74% at end at $33.05, as the price of copper declined.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) slid 2.22% to end at $90.45. The company owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday to sell $38 million at an average of PEN2.776 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol closed slightly weaker at PEN2.776 per dollar compared with PEN2.773 per dollar in the previous trading session.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the sol has appreciated 1.10% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-99927 7269; peru@dowjones.com [ 10-03-11 1626ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 27   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020111003e7a300043\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
