\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  sol falls 1.6 pct in Sept; cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2011\par 20:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quote)\par \par \uc2 LIMA, Sept 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $141 million on Friday, a practice it began last week to prevent volatility as investors dropped high-yielding emerging market assets on concerns of a new global recession.\par \par \uc2 The sol <PEN=PE> still ended the day 0.1 percent weaker at 2.773 per dollar, bringing its losses for the month to 1.6 percent. September has been a rough month for emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar is gaining due to the environment abroad, in line with the other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region," said one local trader.\par \par \uc2 Investors have lost confidence that European debt troubles might soon be resolved, with weak sentiment compounded on Friday by data that showed China's manufacturing sector had contracted again.[ID:nL3E7KU097]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market because half of all deposits in Peru are made in dollars and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility hurts businesses and consumers. Before last week, it had generally bought rather than sold dollars.\par \par \uc2 Since Sept. 22 it has sold $575 million. So far this year the bank has purchased $1.16 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ursula Scollo and Caroline Stauffer; Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-PERU/SOL (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110930e79u001f8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict