\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Market Indexes End Lower; Sol Weaker\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ryan Dube   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2011\par 01:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended lower on Friday, dragged down by international markets on continued concerns about the health of the global economy.\par \par \uc2 The broad General Index closed 0.58% weaker at 18,329.10.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index ended 0.48% lower at 25,552.34.\par \par \uc2 Stocks saw a high degree of volatility in the third quarter on concerns about a debt crisis in Europe and a slowdown in the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange reached a third-quarter high on July 27, a day before President Ollanta Humala took office on improved confidence from investors that the new administration would not make major changes to the economy.\par \par \uc2 However the bourse tumbled in early August, along with other international markets, after \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  downgraded its long-term ratings on U.S. government debt. The Lima Stock Exchange has since continued to be impacted by the outlook for the global economy.\par \par \uc2 "This isn't an issue of domestic policies, it is basically the international situation," Jose Luis Bustamante, the head trader at brokerage Cartisa SAB, said Friday during a telephone interview.\par \par \uc2 The mining-heavy exchange has also been impacted by a decrease in metal prices.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, base metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) closed 1.73% lower at $24.96 as copper prices declined. Silver and lead miner \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLCABC1.VL) ended 2.30% weaker at 2.55 soles ($0.92).\par \par \uc2 Going the other way, financial holding \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP, BAP.VL) gained 1.65% to end at $92.50.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol also saw volatility in the third-quarter as a result of global economic concerns. During the quarter, the Peruvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuated between PEN2.725 per dollar to PEN2.7736.\par \par \uc2 The weakening of the sol came in the last two weeks of September as investors flocked to the U.S. dollar and copper prices declined.\par \par \uc2 The weakening of the sol led the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reverse a trend of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy dollars. On Sept. 22, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $200 million, which was the first time it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars since April 27 this year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  went on to sell a total of $575 million in the final days of September as investor jitters continued to strengthen the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The total includes an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $141 million at an average of PEN2.773 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 While many economists say short-term volatility for the sol may continue, they also expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate in the medium term thanks largely to the strength of the nation's external accounts.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the sol weakened to PEN2.773 per dollar from PEN2.771 in the previous session. The sol has appreciated 1.21% against the greenback so far this year.\par \par \uc2 -By Ryan Dube, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-945 043 802; peru@dowjones.com [ 30-09-11 2300GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110930e79u0019o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
