\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Market Debt,  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Echo Rebound In Risky Markets\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anjali Cordeiro and Cynthia Lin   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2011\par 20:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and credits took a bit of a break from their recent declines Thursday, as so-called risk assets recovered on news that five major central banks are working together to provide liquidity for crisis-embroiled European banks.\par \par \uc2 Latin American and Eastern European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were slightly stronger against the dollar and euro, while sovereign credit spreads tightened with U.S. Treasury yields rising. The joint announcement from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Federal Reserve, and three other key monetary authorities that they are going to coordinate efforts to provide euro-zone banks with dollar funding, lifted investors sentiment.\par \par \uc2 "People are feeling a little better about Europe from the ECB announcement, so emerging markets are largely up," said Win Thin, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 . "But I'm still skeptical because not much about the underlying dynamic has changed."\par \par \uc2 The risk premium, or spread, on the \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Global was six basis points tighter to 385 basis points over Treasurys. In price terms, the index was down 0.23%.\par \par \uc2 Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which rallied early this year, have fallen sharply in recent days due to worries about global growth and contagion from the euro zone's debt problems. Now central banks in these countries are in the position of having to hold them up rather than find ways to weaken them, as was the case earlier in the year.\par \par \uc2 "By year-end, all these guys will probably be cutting rates," Thin said.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate decision is due later Thursday and it is widely expected to keep its target policy rate unchanged at 5.25%. Its spread on the Embig tightened five basis points to 1.59%, but fell a fraction in price terms.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Indonesia was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Traders also said that the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been working on extending stimulus from the fiscal side and said Tuesday that it will adopt measures to speed public sector investments.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia may need to introduce fiscal stimulus next year to help shield its economy from a potential global economic slowdown, senior officials said Thursday. Finance Minister Agus Martowardojo told a parliamentary hearing that the country may need to issue a fiscal stimulus package in the first half of next year.\par \par \uc2 While growth across Asia appears relatively resilient, the outlook in emerging Europe appears to be headed for a slowdown given its ties to the beleaguered euro-zone bloc. The deteriorating sovereign debt problems there are expected to dent the export demand for goods produced by these highly open economies such as Hungary and the Czech Republic.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and credit markets have been coming under excruciating pressure in recent days as investors reel from new government proposals that could hit the country's banks. The forint has fallen particularly hard recently after Prime Minister Viktor Orban announced controversial plans Monday to help struggling households by locking in exchange rates on mortgages denominated in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly Swiss francs.\par \par \uc2 But the forint and Polish zloty recovered ground against the euro Thursday on the coordinated move by the central banks to provide dollar funding to European banks. That alleviates some pressure, for now, that has been mounting for euro-zone banks to raise short-term funding because investors fear their exposure to the region's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The zloty strengthened to PLN4.3284 per euro from PLN4.3809 to start the day, while the forint gained to HUF284.94 a euro from HUF287.06. Emerging Europe's region index on the Embig lost 0.08% in price, while its spread narrowed seven basis points to 3.45%.\par \par \uc2 By Anjali Cordeiro; Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2200; anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -Clare Connaghan contributed to this article. [ 15-09-11 1830GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110915e79f00194\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
