\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Stronger\b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2011\par 22:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Wednesday, lifted by an upgrade in the country's credit status by \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  Rating Service a day earlier.\par \par \uc2 Lima's mining-heavy exchange was also boosted by higher copper prices.\par \par \uc2 The broad General Index closed 3.38% stronger at 20,695.76.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index ended 3.61% higher at 28,886.03.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 , (BAP), which owns Peru's largest bank, rose 3.29% to close at $98.87.\par \par \uc2 Copper mine Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) increased 3.11% to end at $39.80. Base metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) closed 3.69% stronger at $33.70.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, when Peru's market was closed for a holiday, S&P raised the country's credit status to BBB, the second-lowest investment-grade status. In the upgrade, S&P said it expects President Ollanta Humala's new government to maintain Peru's economic growth with policy flexibility.\par \par \uc2 S&P's decision was seen as a surprise, despite Peru's strong macroeconomic indicators, as there is still uncertainty in the new government's microeconomic policies, Banco Continental said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Brokerage Inteligo SAB said the impact of the upgrade on Peru's equity market could last for "some additional time."\par \par \uc2 "It could lure investors to enter a market with strong fundamentals that have been severely chastised by the bleak external picture and by the worries of a government that has proved to be more pragmatic and market friendly than many initially feared," Inteligo said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday to purchase $86 million at an average of PEN2.7268 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase almost $600 million.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 The sol closed slightly stronger Wednesday at PEN2.727 per dollar, compared with PEN2.731 per dollar in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the sol has appreciated 2.85% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -By Ryan Dube, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1 945 043 802; peru@dowjones.com [ 08-31-11 1650ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020110831e78v0007z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
