\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens\b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2011\par 22:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Friday, as various mining companies gained ground following an announcement Thursday about an agreement with the government on a new tax.\par \par \uc2 The broad General Index ended 1.65% stronger at 19,795.94.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index closed 1.72% higher at 27,492.87.\par \par \uc2 Copper producer Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 1.58% to end at $38.60. Base metals mining company \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) rose 1.91% to close at $32.00.\par \par \uc2 Silver and lead mining company \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLCABC1.VL) climbed 3.17% to end at 2.93 soles ($1.07).\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Salomon Lerner Ghitis announced Thursday an agreement with mining companies to implement a new tax that could raise about 3.0 billion soles ($1.1 billion) a year.\par \par \uc2 "While the government gave no details about specific tax changes, the number looks reasonable and indicates that the tax hike will be moderate," the Eurasia Group said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday to purchase $147 million at an average of PEN2.7305 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $224 million Monday, $149 million Tuesday, $50 million Wednesday and $29.7 million Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol closed slightly stronger Friday at PEN2.731 per dollar, compared with PEN2.732 per dollar in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 -By Ryan Dube, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-945 043 802; peru@dowjones.com [ 08-26-11 1654ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110826e78q000ro\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
