\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Market Indexes End Higher; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 232 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2011\par 22:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes closed stronger on Tuesday as various mining companies gained ground boosted by higher metal prices.\par \par \uc2 The broad General Index ended 0.35% higher to end at 22153.70. The blue-chip Selective Index closed 1.47% stronger at 30857.88.\par \par \uc2 Copper producer Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 4.74% to end at $45.30 as the price for the red metal increased. Silver and lead miner \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLCABC1.VL) closed 1.88% higher at 3.25 soles ($1.19).\par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.Vl) increased 1.55% to end at $42.65.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday to purchase $200 million at an average of PEN2.7358 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. On Monday it purchased $12 million.\par \par \uc2 The sol has been under appreciation pressure in recent trading sessions due to demand before the Independence Day holiday as well as due to increased optimism about the incoming government.\par \par \uc2 The sol closed unchanged Tuesday at PEN2.7370 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Ryan Dube, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1 9454 043 802; peru@dowjones.com [ 07-26-11 1653ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 27   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110726e77q00056\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
