\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-EXCLUSIVE-Peru says has economic 'contingency plan'\b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2011\par 00:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Finance minister has plan if markets sell-off\par \par \uc2  * Humala economics adviser pledges stability\par \par \uc2  * Warns of "speculative attack"\par \par \uc2  (Adds quotes, byline)\par \par \uc2  By Patricia Velez\par \par \uc2  LIMA, June 5 (Reuters) - Peru's government has a "contingency plan" ready to implement if markets sink in the event of a victory by leftist Ollanta Humala in Sunday's presidential election, Finance Minister Ismael Benavides said.\par \par \uc2  Humala, a former army officer, has a lead of at least 5 percentage points in three exit polls. He has moderated his anti-capitalist views over the last few years, but many investors still fear he would roll back free-market policies if elected in the fast-growing economy.\par \par \uc2  "We have a contingency plan (which aims to) provide liquidity in the market via the Treasury ... to give a hand to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Benavides told Reuters.\par \par \uc2  Benavides stressed that whoever wins the presidency must quickly move to win the confidence of markets.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Humala's chief economics adviser said stability would be assured if Humala wins but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the country suffers a speculative attack.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stocks <.IGRA> and sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <PEN=PE> have been highly volatile in recent weeks as investors worry that Humala would pursue an \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda in \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fast-growing economy. Analysts said markets could plunge on Monday if Humala is confirmed.\par \par \uc2  "There is no reason to worry, monetary policy will be maintained, responsible fiscal policy will guarantee the sustainability of fiscal accounts," economist Felix Jimenez, who authored Humala's campaign platform, told journalists.\par \par \uc2  Peru has investment grade credit ratings and record       international reserves of $44 billion, equal to about one third of annual gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2  But Jimenez also warned of potential volatility in financial markets.\par \par \uc2  "If there is a speculative attack, I reiterate that I would ask the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do its job. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the instruments to avert a speculative attack," he said shortly after exit polls gave Humala a narrow lead following voting.\par \par \uc2  Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has periodically raised deposit requirements on bank accounts, especially those tied to foreign loans, in a bid to limit speculation on the sol and has sold dollars on the local spot market to prop up the sol.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Julio Velarde told Reuters in April that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was studying ways to respond in case confidence undermined markets. [ID:nN01151534]\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Teresa Cespedes)   \par \par \uc2 PERU-ELECTION/CONTINGENCY (UPDATE 1, EXCLUSIVE)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110608e76500193\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
