\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Peru markets plunge as Fujimori lead narrows\b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2011\par 16:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Note: Election law forbids publication of polls in Peru a week prior to June 5 voting)\par \par \uc2 * Sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ends 0.69 pct weaker; stocks down 5.16 pct\par \par \uc2 * Right-wing Fujimori has slim lead six days from voting\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds commentary)\par \par \uc2 LIMA, May 30 (Reuters) - Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened the most in nine weeks and the local stock index fell sharply on Monday, with traders citing polls showing right-wing lawmaker Keiko Fujimori's lead over left-wing nationalist Ollanta Humala had narrowed ahead of the June 5 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <PEN=PE> closed bidding 0.69 percent weaker, its largest fall since March 28, at 2.769 per U.S. dollar, while stocks <.IGRA> closed down 5.16 percent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, announced an auction for 250 million soles ($89 million) in deposit certificates to soak up the demand for dollars but did not place any of them.\par \par \uc2 "The fall in the market is a response to the polls over the weekend," said Edwin Paz, a trader at local stock brokerage Provalor in Lima.\par \par \uc2 Fujimori leads Humala, who has tried with limited success to campaign as a moderate and distance himself from his former political mentor, Venezuela's socialist President Hugo Chavez. Fujimori's lead ranges between 1 point and 4.6 points in four polls. For more see [ID:nN27173077].\par \par \uc2 Investors worry Humala would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the economy, one of the world's fastest-growing, and hurt private investment. They trust Fujimori because they credit her father, former President Alberto Fujimori, with opening the economy in the 1990s. He is in jail for corruption and human rights abuse.\par \par \uc2 Peru's stock index plunged 21 percent between March 24 and April 27 on fears Humala would win. Markets have since recovered as Fujimori surpassed the former army officer in polls but will likely be volatile until the June 5 run-off vote.\par \par \uc2 With polls showing a small margin between the two candidates, \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  wrote in a research note that the election could go to a recount, delaying the results.\par \par \uc2 "Investors should be prepared for high market volatility as the political system sorts out the vote recount process and manages the ensuing conflicts of interest," the report said.\par \par \uc2 Shares in Buenaventura , the largest precious metals miner in Peru, a top metals producer, were down 4.52 percent, while shares in Southern Copper shed 6.85 percent on the local bourse.\par \par \uc2 U.S. markets were closed for a holiday.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ursula Scollo; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-PERU (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110530e75u000wx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
