\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-Peru  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  seen hiking rate to 4.25 pct\b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2011\par 21:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WHAT: Peru's interest rate decision\par \par \uc2 WHEN: Thursday, May 12, around 7 p.m. EST (2300 GMT)\par \par \uc2 OUTCOME: Rate seen rising 25 basis points to 4.25 pct\par \par \uc2 REUTERS FORECAST: Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday is expected to raise its benchmark interest rate <PECPI=ECI> by 25 basis points for a fifth straight month after April inflation beat market expectations, according to all 10 economists surveyed by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Consumer prices in Peru rose 0.68 percent in April, barely off their 0.7 percent increase in March, the fastest in nearly three years. Higher international commodities prices have pushed Peru's 12-month inflation above the bank's 1 to 3 percent target range. Food is the largest component of Peru's monthly inflation calculation.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has indicated a "neutral" monetary policy would put the rate at 4.5 percent, suggesting more hikes could be in store. \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said in a research note the tightening cycle will likely continue until July, which would put the benchmark at 4.75 percent by mid-year.\par \par \uc2 MARKET IMPACT: Seen minimal. A higher interest rate can increase the demand for Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <PEN=PE>, but the sol has traded on the uncertainty of a presidential election in the past two months. It had weakened around 1 percent against the U.S. dollar in the two weeks after nationalist candidate Ollanta Humala won the first round vote on April 10. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained in the past week as three different pollsters showed right-wing lawmaker Keiko Fujimori gaining to a statistical tie with Humala. \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly on the local spot market to prevent sharp volatility that hurts businesses and consumers in a country where half of bank deposits are made in dollars.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ursula Scollo; Writing by Caroline Stauffer; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 PERU-ECONOMY/RATES (PREVIEW)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110513e75a002yf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
