\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Peru's Markets Bearing Brunt Of Political Worries\b0\par\par\uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2011\par 22:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds stock market closing figures, and closing and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures for sol.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Robert Kozak \par     Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's political uncertainty is undermining the strength of its once robust financial markets, knocking the stock market down from lofty levels, swelling its bond spreads and weakening its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Concerns about the prospects for Peru's policies have increased following the rise in political support for left-leaning nationalist Ollanta Humala, who took the most votes in the April 10 election for president and who is leading in opinion polls before the June 5 runoff.\par \par \uc2 Humala, 48, and his contender, center-right Congresswoman Keiko Fujimori, 35, both favor placing a windfall tax on mining companies. Humala also hopes to modify Peru's constitution, in part to give the state a greater role in the economy. Fujimori, daughter of jailed ex-president Alberto Fujimori, says she will keep Peru on the same market-friendly policies followed in the last two decades.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index, which gained 65% last year, has tumbled some 28% so far this year, with a decline of 19% this month to the end of trade on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the General Index ended 1.09% higher due to bargain hunting and heavy volumes in trade of one blue-chip mining company.\par \par \uc2 The stock market, which is heavily reliant on mining companies, has weakened despite strong prices for many of the minerals that the companies mine in Peru.\par \par \uc2 "Peru has become one of the worst performing stock markets in the world and that is because of concerns about Mr. Humala," said Cesar Perez-Novoa, a managing director with Celfin Capital. "You will see a lot of volatility," he added.\par \par \uc2 A robust economy--gross domestic product expanded by 8.8% last year--and solid government and private sector company finances have helped boost interest in investing in Peru, which has an investment grade debt rating.\par \par \uc2 The free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol, which has been on an appreciating trend in the last few years, has depreciated by 0.86% against the U.S. dollar this year, to the end of Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $8.96 billion last year as inflows of cash strengthened the sol, has changed direction. On April 14, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell $91 million, the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell since February 2009.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell $492 million, although the sol ended slightly weaker at PEN2.831 per dollar, compared with PEN2.830 per dollar in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the slide in the sol and local stocks, Peruvian bond spreads have been widening.\par \par \uc2 "With opinion polls suggesting that the second round of voting will be a close call, Peruvian markets have sold off sharply," Capital Economics said in a Wednesday research note. "The principal concern is that if Mr. Humala prevails he will pursue a program of economic nationalism that will squeeze foreign firms, particularly in the mining sector."\par \par \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  said in a report it was keeping its short position in the sol unless political developments or poll results suggest Fujimori could win the presidency. "Keeping a defensive exposure still pays, in our view," it added.\par \par \uc2 When Humala ran unsuccessfully for office in 2006 against President Alan Garcia, he was closely tied to Venezuela's socialist firebrand President Hugo Chavez.\par \par \uc2 In this election Humala has moderated his policies in speeches and press conferences, but his party's official governing plan remains a hard-line manifesto that promises a "Grand Transformation" of Peru's society and economy.\par \par \uc2 "Our recent baseline assumption had been one of likely political continuity, but the odds have changed in the last month, raising the potential for dramatic political change," \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  said in a commentary.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-99927 7269; peru@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -0- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 04-27-11 1632ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110427e74r000yt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
