\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Peru central bank \highlight\uc2  pulled into election volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2011\par 21:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily\par \par \uc2 * Traders say sol responding to local factors (Recasts, adds quotes, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 LIMA, April 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times on Wednesday in an attempt to curb the slide in the sol <PEN=PE> as investors dumped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on concerns left-wing Ollanta Humala could win the presidential election on June 5.\par \par \uc2 Peruvian financial assets have been under pressure this week after a poll released on Sunday showed Humala leads the race against right-wing lawmaker Keiko Fujimori. For details, see [ID:nN24168504]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed 750 million soles ($178.57 million) in deposit certificates in two separate auctions designed to absorb demand for dollars. It then sold $492 million dollars.\par \par \uc2 The sol <PEN=PE> closed bidding 0.07 percent weaker at 2.83 per dollar on the local spot market after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , snapping back from 2.836, its weakest level of the session.\par \par \uc2 "The market is moving mostly on internal politics and the uncertainty of the election rather than factors abroad," said one trader who declined to be named.\par \par \uc2 The sol was a bit of an anomaly among Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican and Chilean pesos <MXN=> <CLP=CL> strengthened after the U.S. Federal Reserve signaled it would keep borrowing costs low for an extended period, favoring higher yielding emerging market assets.\par \par \uc2 "Peru is the exception," the IDEAglobal consultancy said in a report.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Peru's benchmark stock index <.IGRA> rose 1.29 percent after falling 2.26 percent on Tuesday, when it closed at its weakest levels since Sept. 29. Traders said it was a technical recovery as the index is down 18 percent since its March 31 close.\par \par \uc2 The sol has weakened around 1 percent this month.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to avert volatility that hurts consumers and businesses as half of the economy is dollarized and many people get paid in one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but owe debts in the other.\par \par \uc2 A weaker sol could also pressure inflation, which was near a three-year high in March and expected to be 0.5 percent in April. [ID:nN2615804]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annual inflation target range is 1 to 3 percent and many economists expect inflation to be above 3 percent this year as global food prices surge.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Teresa Cespedes and Caroline Stauffer)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-PERU/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110501e74r000bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
