\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt, Sells $492 Million\b0\par\par\uc2 165 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2011\par 20:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, selling $492 million at an average price of PEN2.8334 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the second time since Feb. 20, 2009 made by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On April 14 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell $91 million.\par \par \uc2 The sol has come under depreciation pressure since the April 10 election that saw left-leaning nationalist leader Ollanta Humala take a first round victory. Humala is in a runoff for the presidency with Congresswoman Keiko Fujimori; the vote will take place June 5.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year purchased $8.96 billion to ease the sol's appreciating trend. It last purchased dollars on Feb. 11.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-99927 7269; peru@dowjones.com [ 27-04-11 1909GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110427e74r001oc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
