\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Slightly Weaker\b0\par\par\uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2011\par 00:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's broad stock market index recovered slightly Wednesday, after two days of election-related declines ahead of a June 5 runoff vote for a new president.\par \par \uc2 "Today there was a bit of a technical correction on bargain hunting for cheap shares and gains in U.S. markets," said Jorge Ramirez, trader with brokerage Coril SAB. Despite the correction, Ramirez said he expected a similar pattern of losses followed by some gains to continue right up until the election.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index ended higher by 1.09% at 17959.32, having lost 2.26% on Tuesday and 3.31% on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Peru's other main index, the Selective blue-chip, also rose slightly Wednesday to close up 1.22% at 24825.18, having lost 2.25% on Tuesday and 3.46% on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Stocks gaining value Wednesday included silver miner Sociedad Minera El Brocal SAA. (BROCALC1.VL), which rose 2.78% to close at 37.00 soles ($13.12), while fellow silver and zinc producer, Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLCABC1.VL), gained 2.71% in heavy trade to close at PEN2.65.\par \par \uc2 Precious metals mining company \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura SA\uc2  (BVN, BUENAVC1.VL) was also higher, up 1.33% to close at $38.00.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way was base metals \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO.VL), down 0.98% to end at $35.40.\par \par \uc2 In the financial sector, holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP), which owns Peru's largest bank, also lost, down 0.90% to end at $88.20.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, selling $492 million at an average price of PEN2.8334 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the second since Feb. 20, 2009. On April 14, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell $91 million.\par \par \uc2 The sol has come under depreciation pressure since the first round April 10 election that saw left-leaning nationalist leader Ollanta Humala take an initial victory.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. Last year it purchased $8.96 billion to ease the sol's appreciating trend. It last purchased dollars on Feb. 11.\par \par \uc2 Following the invention the sol closed slightly weaker Wednesday at PEN2.831 per U.S. dollar, compared to the previous close of PEN2.830.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; +51-989 038 043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 04-27-11 1811ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110427e74r0006t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
