\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol A Bit Weaker\b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2011\par 22:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's stock market continued to recover Friday, closing higher on bargain hunting and stronger gold prices.\par \par \uc2 This week the main index lost almost 9%, compared to last Friday's close, following a market selloff in the first part of the week triggered by news that left-leaning nationalist leader Ollanta Humala had won a first-round victory in Sunday's presidential elections. Humala is in a runoff vote for president with congresswoman Keiko Fujimori, which is scheduled to take place June 5.\par \par \uc2 Buyers finally returned to the market at the end of the week to bargain hunt, said analysts.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index ended 3.42% higher to close at 19371.26. On Monday, the index fell 3.10%, followed by a 3.58% decline Tuesday and a 6.22% fall Wednesday. On Thursday, it closed up 0.63%.\par \par \uc2 Peru's other main index, the Selective blue-chip, ended 2.88% higher Friday at 26605.02. On Thursday, the index closed up 0.17%, but was 5.13% lower Wednesday, 3.54% weaker on Tuesday and 3.33% lower on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Stocks gaining value Friday included precious metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.Vl), which closed 1.81% higher at $39.30, in line with stronger gold prices.\par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) was up 2.67% to end at $38.50. At one point on Thursday Cerro Verde had lost about 14%.\par \par \uc2 Base metals miner \uc2 Compania Minera Milpo\uc2  SAA (MILPOC1.VL) also gained, in line with news it had won a $400 million copper mine concession from the Peruvian government, rising 2.71% to close at 6.45 soles ($2.30).\par \par \uc2 In the financial sector, holding \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2  (BAP) was up 1.54% to close at $95.50.\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market the sol ended Friday's session slightly weaker at PEN2.823 per U.S. dollar. The sol ended the previous session at PEN2.822 per dollar, after \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell $91 million.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol has strengthened by 0.46% against the greenback over a 12-month period.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany, Dow Jones Newswires; +51-989 038 043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 04-15-11 1643ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110415e74f000cn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
