\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Peru assets fall, candidate worries traders\b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 16:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Nationalist Humala clenches narrow lead in April 10 race\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakens, CDS rise 12 basis points\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to blunt demand for dollars\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds commentary)\par \par \uc2 LIMA, March 28 (Reuters) - Peru's sol closed at its weakest levels in more than three months on Monday as nationalist presidential candidate Ollanta Humala, who now has a narrow lead, failed to pacify traders with his more moderate message.\par \par \uc2 The sol <PEN=PE> closed 0.93 percent weaker at 2.816 against the dollar, its greatest intraday fall this year. One local trader said he saw opportunities to bet on swings in the now volatile Peruvian market.\par \par \uc2 Humala has gained in polls by toning down radical rhetoric that hurt him in the 2006 race. On Monday he promised to respect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authority and honor trade agreements as president in the most moderate speech of his political career.[ID:nN28200405]\par \par \uc2 But his ascent in polls by Ipsos Apoyo and CPI consultancies has still rattled markets and investors worry about his proposals to raise taxes on the country's vast mining industry and renegotiate terms of some contracts.\par \par \uc2 "Peruvian asset prices are likely to become more volatile in the coming two weeks," wrote Nomura economist Benito Berber in a research note. "This is in line with what happened prior to the previous presidential election where (sol) volatility peaked one week before the first round."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered in three separate auctions to sell a contract to help soak up the demand for dollars and sold 300 million soles ($107 million) of the instrument.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize the local spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because half of the bank deposits made in Peru are in dollars and volatility hurts businesses and consumers.\par \par \uc2 STOCKS DOWN NEARLY 5 PERCENT\par \par \uc2 Peru's benchmark stock index <.IGRA> fell 4.73 percent, hurt by falling metals prices as well as the polls. Peru is a top metals producer and shares in mining companies are a large component of the local bourse.\par \par \uc2 "The market's losses are due to electoral uncertainty, and on top of this we are seeing a fall in the prices of raw materials," said one trader in Lima who declined to be named because of the small local market.\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring Peruvian debt rose 12 basis points to 137 <PEGV5YUSAC=> while Peru debt spreads widened 5 basis points to 168, according to \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 's Emerging Markets Bond Index <11EMJ>.\par \par \uc2 Pollsters say Humala's more moderate image has allowed him to nab support from former President Alejandro Toledo, who had been the front-runner in the race but is now trailing Humala by a couple of percentage points.\par \par \uc2 Despite the market's jitters, polls show Humala would likely lose in a June 5 runoff to any one of his four potential rivals, all of whom are more trusted by investors. [ID:nN27252905]\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ursula Scollo and Caroline Stauffer; Editing by Kenneth Barry)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-PERU/ (UPDATE 3)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110328e73s00126\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
